    "updated_at": "2022-04-05T14:29:43Z",
    "body": "> No. It demonstrates how to set scoped environment variables, and thus are not meant to include the starship timings part.\r\n\r\nBut the following line is literally included in the documentation and *does* include the timings part.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nenv STARSHIP_LOG=trace starship timings\r\n```\r\n\r\n> As specific logs files are used for deduplicating log messages, you might also want to set STARSHIP_SESSION_KEY, [like the official init does](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/init/starship.nu?rgh-link-date=2022-04-05T14%3A18%3A38Z#L2).\r\n\r\nThanks. I took mine from https://www.nushell.sh/book/3rdpartyprompts.html#starship but I'll have a look at that one too.",
